# emotion — the outcome, not the verb.
#
# Copied from cli/outcome/coin_grant/success.cli, which is a known-good pickpocket run, and changed
# in exactly three ways: --grant-mm avarice makes the disposition present (the starting kit is
# random, so without it whether the protagonist HOLDS an emotion modus mentis is a coin flip), one
# extra `advance` drains the emotion's own preview part, and the assertions read the spleen.
#
# What it proves, and why each half is needed: `expect-outcome emotion` says the emotion really ran
# (its chip is coloured from the humor's vital heat and carries a count, so scanning the screen for
# one would be asserting a rendering); `inspect humors` says the spleen actually moved, which is the
# only thing that distinguishes a chip from a change. The spleen starts pure Blood at creation, so
# any other humor name in the spleen line is the emotion having landed.
#
# It does NOT assert WHICH humor. The protagonist may hold more than one disposition that answers a
# coin — greed and thrift both do — and the resolver samples one of the matches, so the humor is
# seed-stable but not scenario-stable, and pinning it would break the day the starting kit changes.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only "brewer" --grant-mm avarice

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# --- before ---
# Creation fills the queues by SECRETION (blood / phlegm / yellow bile, plus seeded juvenescence), so
# the spleen is not empty - what it has none of is a mind state, and that is the assertion.
inspect humors
expect-no-state humors Voluptas

strategy succeed
goal pickpocket
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

# The emotional coda is a preview part of its own, so it needs its own press. `advance` settles and
# drains whatever is up, which is a no-op on the runs where nothing was felt.
advance 12 180

# --- the outcome really ran ---
expect-outcome coin_grant
expect-outcome emotion

# --- the player was told, in the emotion modus mentis's own voice ---
# Under --playground the persona rewrite returns the neutral line unchanged, so the humor's own
# FeelsLike sentence is on screen verbatim. This is the block, not the chip: it proves the coda was
# narrated and committed, which the chip alone does not.
expect It makes me feel

# --- after: the spleen really moved ---
# Nothing but EmotionOutcome.Apply can put a mind state in a queue - secretion never produces one.
inspect humors
expect-state humors Voluptas
quit
